tantivy-go.test
# Cargo.lock IS committed in this fork. Upstream ignores it because the crate
# is a library, but here it is the input to a static library that gets pinned by
# SHA-256 and linked into a service that reads every tenant's corpus: without a
# lock, 'the same commit' can produce a different binary.
!rust/Cargo.lock
